I believe that I also ascended my first monk, although I am not hundred 
percent sure (this was of course not NH3.1.3, and I didn't keep the log 
files from later).  Anyway, monks are easy in the beginning and more 
difficult in the end.  Which means that an experienced player like you 
will not have too many problems when going for a first-try ascencion :-).

I am currently trying a slash'em monk.  They are even easier than 
nethack ones, because they hit harder and get better intrinsic AC with 
increasing level.  I lost one, but to a game crash; this game keeps 
crashing, but now I am prepared, making a backup file after each first 
change to a new level.  Tedious, but being "killed" by a "trickery" 
after having disposed of Demogorgon is no fun... (and you have no option 
of recovery, because the game exits "gracefully" by asking you whether 
you want your possessions identified... I would prefer a hard crash with 
recover working afterwards).  In slashem, I believe monks to be the 
easiest class, and they can get AC from body armor as well, since a robe 
is worn as body armor but does not interfere with spell-casting, n or 
reduce the monks fighting capabilities.  So they are even easier than 
barbarians.  (I lost one barbarian to a stupid mistake and another one 
that had killed Demo to a game crash.)

What I will definitely not try is to kill Demogorgon by hand as you did. 
  Even with Elbereth this does not seem advisable (I think he is 
stronger in slashem than in NH); I will use firearms, when the time 
comes.  In wizard mode I even managed once to take him down with a 
single salvo of seven +7 bullets.  The advantage of having Demogorgon in 
a lair is of course that you can choose your battle ground.

